Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

Attached is a good explanation of PE fusions and sources of poor fusions.  =
Please read it.

In the report you will see "cold fusion" discussed which is one of the buzz=
 words used by CMF's Doug Zak to rationalize the Polygate failures (that is=
 assigning their cause to installation error).  He also uses this as a scar=
e tactic to help sell the "single source" from CMF strategy.  He coaches co=
nsultants on how to use this to pitch their customers on this as a useful t=
radeoff for competitive bidding.  Eric Christiansen in particular.

You will see the reference to SCG (they call it "stress crack growth").  In=
 US we call it "slow crack growth".  It's the same thing.  You will see rem=
arks that almost all PE failures are due to this.

Get familiar and used to this term.

J

